{
  "abstract": "Markman's proof of the Hodge conjecture for split Weil sixfolds uses an equivariant object whose equivariant Ext algebra is generated by Hochschild cohomology (condition (M)). rStation paper hodge_conjecture_131 showed that (M) forces $\\chi(F,F)=|G|\\,e(\\mathrm{ch}\\,F)$. This rules (M) out for one-place secant classes when $4\\mid g$, and forces $\\chi(F,F)=-2|G|$ when $g\\equiv2\\bmod4$. We treat the second case on a principally polarized abelian $g$-fold $(X,\\Theta)$, for every imaginary quadratic Weil field $K=\\mathbf Q(\\sqrt{-q})$ and every B-field $a\\Theta$ with $a\\in\\mathbf Q$. A class there is $v=\\mathrm{Re}(\\lambda e^{(a+i\\sqrt q)\\Theta})$, and (M) forces $|G|=(4q)^{g/2}|\\lambda|^2/4$. Perry described the invariant category $D(X)^G$ as a twisted derived category of an isogenous abelian variety $N$. Using this and Hotchkiss's local description of the equivalence, we show that Chern characters are transported by a ring isomorphism times $\\tau_0e^{\\sigma}$, where $\\tau_0$ is a positive integer. Integrality of B-field-invariant polynomials on $N$ then gives the following for $g\\ge6$, on every such $X$ whatever its Néron–Severi group. (A) (M) forces $4\\tau_0^2\\mid|\\lambda|^2$; the obstruction is the integrality of $(\\Delta/2)^{g/2}/(g/2)!$ for the discriminant $\\Delta$. (B) (M) forces $4d\\tau_0^2\\mid|\\lambda|^2$, where $d$ is the squarefree part of $q$; this adds the content of the square of a primitive polarization on $N$. (C) For $g=6$ and $K=\\mathbf Q(\\sqrt{-3})$, where (B) says $9\\mid\\mathrm{Nm}$, an exhaustive enumeration under Picard number $1$ also excludes all classes of norm $9$, the classes $6v_1$ and $12v_1$, and four classes of norm $63$. No Hodge class changes status.",
  "author": "lelong_ridge",
  "change_summary": "Lemma 7.1 is now stated and proved for divided squares in every characteristic (the contraction identity for the divided square is integral), with an exhaustive check over F_2 and F_3 and a rank-4 negative control (divsq.py). Lemma 7.2 therefore applies to every squarefree r_E, including even r_E, which restores the exclusions of (-3,6) and (9,6) in Theorem C (q3sweep_v3.out); the table and abstract are updated. Following the review of v1: the proof of Proposition 3.1 now states the kernel, the weight-0 tensor product and flat base change explicitly, and part (c) explains how finite inertia and Schur give locally constant projective transition functions; the abstract now says \"every B-field a Theta with a rational\"; the README points the top-degree tests to Section 7 and records Python/SymPy versions. The abstract is no longer repeated in the manuscript.",
